Golden SafePlcIO=1 refuses to run unless SnAllSafeDoor and SnAllEMG are both enabled (bCheckPLCAllSafedoorAndEMGEnable, G14: SystemStart=false + StopAllMotor every pass) and raises WAR16125 from SnAllSafeDoor. This machine's MOSAIC project has one input per door and no combined bit, so W906_PlcM1SAllDoors (end of MyPLC/MyPLC_IO_Modbus.cpp) sets InPortData_Byte[17] bit 0 only when every door of golden's iSafeDoor[] list that the IO table puts on the PLC reads closed in the same frame; no PLC door -> 0, a door outside the 16 input bytes -> open. Per-door alarms stay golden's. Same-line call/declaration; only active with SafePlcModel=1.

tests/test_myplc_modbus.cpp [5]: 64/64. Debug 19:12, release 19:13. Backup branch backup/pre-plcdoor-20261006. The IO_Table renumbering to the software door positions and SafePlcIO=1 are NOT in this commit (machine data, left for EastSun).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
